{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>כאשר לא נגענוך and as etc.</b> A parable: a lion had a bone stuck in its throat. It said: whoever comes and removes it, the king will make him very wealthy. A certain bird named agron, whose neck is long, came and said: I will remove it. The bird inserted its head into the lion's throat and extracted the bone. After it extracted it, it asked for its reward. The lion said to it: Is it not enough for you that I sent you away in peace and did not eat you when you inserted your head into my throat — but you still ask for a reward? Thus Avimelekh said to Yitzchak: We did you a great kindness in that we sent you away in peace, for our way is to harm all comers."], :book :genesis, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:06:05.622312762Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}